  },
  {
    "objectID": "01_intro.html#clean-the-environment",
    "href": "01_intro.html#clean-the-environment",
    "title": "1  Introduction",
    "section": "1.2 Clean the environment",
    "text": "1.2 Clean the environment\n\n# List all objects in the environment\nls()\n\n[1] \"pandoc_dir\"      \"quarto_bin_path\"\n\n# Remove all objects from the environment\nrm(list = ls())\n\n# Verify the change\nls()\n\ncharacter(0)",
    "crumbs": [
      "<span class='chapter-number'>1</span>  <span class='chapter-title'>Introduction</span>"
    ]
  },
  {
    "objectID": "01_intro.html#basic-r-programming-concepts",
    "href": "01_intro.html#basic-r-programming-concepts",
    "title": "1  Introduction",
    "section": "1.3 Basic R Programming Concepts",
    "text": "1.3 Basic R Programming Concepts\n\n# This is a comment\n\n# Create object \"number\"\n\nnumber &lt;- 5\n\n\n# Print the object in the console:\n\nnumber\n\n[1] 5\n\n\n# Define the function \"square()\"\n\nsquare &lt;- function(x) { return(x^2) }\n\n# Run function on object, store as \"result\"\n\nresult &lt;- square(number)\n\n# Print the result in the console\n\nprint(result)",
    "crumbs": [
      "<span class='chapter-number'>1</span>  <span class='chapter-title'>Introduction</span>"
    ]
  },
  {
    "objectID": "01_intro.html#r-packages",
    "href": "01_intro.html#r-packages",
    "title": "1  Introduction",
    "section": "1.4 R Packages",
    "text": "1.4 R Packages\n# Install once (downloads from CRAN)\ninstall.packages(\"ggplot2\")\n# Load every time you start R\nlibrary(ggplot2)",
    "crumbs": [
      "<span class='chapter-number'>1</span>  <span class='chapter-title'>Introduction</span>"
    ]
  },
  {
    "objectID": "01_intro.html#r-objects",
    "href": "01_intro.html#r-objects",
    "title": "1  Introduction",
    "section": "1.5 R Objects",
    "text": "1.5 R Objects\n# generate objects\nn &lt;- 100 # Scalar object\nid &lt;- 1:n # Vector object\nage &lt;- sample(18:65, n, replace = TRUE)\n\n# Visualize\nage # Print object in console\nstr(age) # Object type, size\nclass(age) # Object type\ndim(age)\nls() # List all objects",
    "crumbs": [
      "<span class='chapter-number'>1</span>  <span class='chapter-title'>Introduction</span>"
    ]
  },
  {
    "objectID": "01_intro.html#vectors",
    "href": "01_intro.html#vectors",
    "title": "1  Introduction",
    "section": "1.6 Vectors",
    "text": "1.6 Vectors\n# Three vectors with one value per month\npassengers &lt;- as.numeric(AirPassengers)\nyear       &lt;- as.numeric(floor(time(AirPassengers)))\nmonth      &lt;- as.numeric(cycle(AirPassengers))\n\nlength(passengers)     # 144\n\n# Access elements of a vector\npassengers[1]          # first element: 112\npassengers[1:3]        # elements 1 to 3: 112 118 132\npassengers[c(1, 144)]  # first and last: 112 432\n\n# Create a dataset from the three vectors\ndf_air &lt;- data.frame(year, month, passengers)\ndim(df_air)            # 144 rows, 3 columns",
    "crumbs": [
      "<span class='chapter-number'>1</span>  <span class='chapter-title'>Introduction</span>"
    ]
  },
  {
    "objectID": "01_intro.html#from-vectors-to-a-dataframes",
    "href": "01_intro.html#from-vectors-to-a-dataframes",
    "title": "1  Introduction",
    "section": "1.7 From Vectors to a Dataframes",
    "text": "1.7 From Vectors to a Dataframes\nhead(df_air)\n  year month passengers\n1 1949     1        112\n2 1949     2        118\n3 1949     3        132\n4 1949     4        129\n5 1949     5        121\n6 1949     6        135",
    "crumbs": [
      "<span class='chapter-number'>1</span>  <span class='chapter-title'>Introduction</span>"
    ]
  },
  {
    "objectID": "01_intro.html#multiple-data-frames",
    "href": "01_intro.html#multiple-data-frames",
    "title": "1  Introduction",
    "section": "1.8 Multiple Data Frames",
    "text": "1.8 Multiple Data Frames\n# longley: US macroeconomic data, one row per year (1947-1962)\ndata(longley)\nclass(longley)        # \"data.frame\"\nhead(longley)\n     GNP.deflator     GNP Unemployed Armed.Forces Population Year Employed\n1947         83.0 234.289      235.6        159.0    107.608 1947   60.323\n1948         88.5 259.426      232.5        145.6    108.632 1948   61.122\n1949         88.2 258.054      368.2        161.6    109.773 1949   60.171\n1950         89.5 284.599      335.1        165.0    110.929 1950   61.187\n1951         96.2 328.975      209.9        309.9    112.075 1951   63.221\n1952         98.1 346.999      193.2        359.4    113.270 1952   63.639",
    "crumbs": [
      "<span class='chapter-number'>1</span>  <span class='chapter-title'>Introduction</span>"
    ]
  },
  {
    "objectID": "01_intro.html#accessing-data---selecting-observations-and-variables",
    "href": "01_intro.html#accessing-data---selecting-observations-and-variables",
    "title": "1  Introduction",
    "section": "1.9 Accessing data - Selecting Observations and Variables",
    "text": "1.9 Accessing data - Selecting Observations and Variables\ndf$age # Print the age column of df\ndf[[2]] # Same as previous line\n# Accessing data through row/column indexes\ndf[1:3,] # Rows 1 to 3, all columns.\ndf[,c(1,4)] # All rows, Columns 1 and 4.\ndf[c(1,25),c(1,3)] # Rows 1 and 25, Columns 1 and 3.\ndf_first_fifty_rows &lt;- df[1:50,]",
    "crumbs": [
      "<span class='chapter-number'>1</span>  <span class='chapter-title'>Introduction</span>"
    ]
  },
  {
    "objectID": "01_intro.html#accessing-data---logical-operators",
    "href": "01_intro.html#accessing-data---logical-operators",
    "title": "1  Introduction",
    "section": "1.10 Accessing data - Logical Operators",
    "text": "1.10 Accessing data - Logical Operators\n# Logical condition vector\nindex_old_males &lt;- (df$gender == \"Male\") & (df$age &gt; 50)\ntable(index_old_males)\ndf_old_males &lt;- df[index_old_males, ]\ndf_old_males &lt;- df[(df$gender == \"Male\") & (df$age &gt; 50), ]",
    "crumbs": [
      "<span class='chapter-number'>1</span>  <span class='chapter-title'>Introduction</span>"
    ]
  },
  {
    "objectID": "01_intro.html#transforming-variables-in-a-data-frame",
    "href": "01_intro.html#transforming-variables-in-a-data-frame",
    "title": "1  Introduction",
    "section": "1.11 Transforming variables in a Data Frame",
    "text": "1.11 Transforming variables in a Data Frame\ndataframe$var1 &lt;- NULL\n# New variables generation\ndf$log_age &lt;- log(df$age)\ndf$is_higly_educated &lt;- df$education %in% c(\"Master\", \"PhD\")",
    "crumbs": [
      "<span class='chapter-number'>1</span>  <span class='chapter-title'>Introduction</span>"
    ]
  },
  {
    "objectID": "01_intro.html#plotting-data-with-ggplot2",
    "href": "01_intro.html#plotting-data-with-ggplot2",
    "title": "1  Introduction",
    "section": "1.12 Plotting Data with ggplot2",
    "text": "1.12 Plotting Data with ggplot2\ninstall.packages(\"ggplot2\")\nlibrary(ggplot2)\n# Histogram of income\nggplot(df, aes(x = income)) +\n  geom_histogram(bins = 30) +\n  labs(x = \"Income\", y = \"Frequency\")\n# Scatterplot of income against age\nggplot(df, aes(x = income, y = age)) +\n  geom_point(size  = 2) +\n  labs(x = \"Income\", y = \"Age\")",
    "crumbs": [
      "<span class='chapter-number'>1</span>  <span class='chapter-title'>Introduction</span>"
    ]
  },
  {
    "objectID": "01_intro.html#histogram",
    "href": "01_intro.html#histogram",
    "title": "1  Introduction",
    "section": "1.13 Histogram",
    "text": "1.13 Histogram\nggplot(df, aes(x = income)) +\n  geom_histogram(bins = 20)\nggplot(df, aes(x = income)) +\n  geom_histogram(bins = 20) +\n  facet_wrap(~ gender, ncol = 1)",
    "crumbs": [
      "<span class='chapter-number'>1</span>  <span class='chapter-title'>Introduction</span>"
    ]
  },
  {
    "objectID": "01_intro.html#bar-chart",
    "href": "01_intro.html#bar-chart",
    "title": "1  Introduction",
    "section": "1.14 Bar Chart",
    "text": "1.14 Bar Chart\nggplot(df, aes(x = education)) +\n  geom_bar()\nggplot(df, aes(x = education, fill = gender)) +\n  geom_bar(position = \"dodge\") +\n  theme(legend.position = \"bottom\")",
    "crumbs": [
      "<span class='chapter-number'>1</span>  <span class='chapter-title'>Introduction</span>"
    ]
  },
  {
    "objectID": "01_intro.html#box-plot",
    "href": "01_intro.html#box-plot",
    "title": "1  Introduction",
    "section": "1.15 Box Plot",
    "text": "1.15 Box Plot\nggplot(df, aes(x = education, y = income)) +\n  geom_boxplot()\nggplot(df, aes(x = education, y = income,\n               fill = gender)) +\n  geom_boxplot() +\n  theme(legend.position = \"bottom\")",
    "crumbs": [
      "<span class='chapter-number'>1</span>  <span class='chapter-title'>Introduction</span>"
    ]
  },
  {
    "objectID": "01_intro.html#scatter-plot",
    "href": "01_intro.html#scatter-plot",
    "title": "1  Introduction",
    "section": "1.16 Scatter Plot",
    "text": "1.16 Scatter Plot\nggplot(df, aes(x = age, y = income)) +\n  geom_point()\nggplot(df, aes(x = age, y = income,\n               colour = gender)) +\n  geom_point() +\n  geom_smooth(method = \"lm\", se = FALSE)",
    "crumbs": [
      "<span class='chapter-number'>1</span>  <span class='chapter-title'>Introduction</span>"
    ]
  },
  {
    "objectID": "01_intro.html#line-graph",
    "href": "01_intro.html#line-graph",
    "title": "1  Introduction",
    "section": "1.17 Line Graph",
    "text": "1.17 Line Graph\nggplot(df_ts[df_ts$country == \"A\", ],\n       aes(x = year, y = unemp)) +\n  geom_line()\nggplot(df_ts, aes(x = year, y = unemp,\n                  colour = country)) +\n  geom_line()",
    "crumbs": [
      "<span class='chapter-number'>1</span>  <span class='chapter-title'>Introduction</span>"
    ]
